 (2026). https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.PENDING-literature","title":"ORCHID literature values","url":"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.PENDING-literature","version":"2026.10"},"contexts":{"doi:10.1016/j.intermet.2012.04.012":{"context_id":"context:source-doi-10-1016-j-intermet-2012-04-012","items":[{"extraction_accepted":false,"has_dropped_fields":true,"id":"ORC-KOH6PMDA2V","instrument":"JEOL JSM 7001F field emission scanning electron microscope (SEM), equipped with a Bruker Quantax energy dispersive X-ray spectroscopy (EDS) system","page":2,"quote":"The phase compositions of the alloys were analyzed using a JEOL JSM 7001F field emission scanning electron microscope (SEM), equipped with a Bruker Quantax energy dispersive X-ray spectroscopy (EDS) system.","second_reader_agrees":false,"type":"measurement"},{"extraction_accepted":true,"id":"ORC-ODXNTEF3F7","instrument":"Bruker D8 X-ray diffractometer","method":"XRD","page":2,"quote":"For XRD analysis, the samples were measured using a Bruker D8 X-ray diffractometer.","second_reader_agrees":true,"type":"measurement"},{"atmosphere":"Helium, at a flow rate of 2 l/h","calibration":"pure Cu, Ag and Mg sealed in tantalum capsules","crucible":"tantalum capsules","extraction_accepted":true,"heating_or_cooling_rate":"þ10 K/ min and then cooled down/heated up in the following cycles:  5 K/ min, þ5 K/min,  1 K/min and þ1 K/min","id":"ORC-SQVFKTG7II","instrument":"heat-flux cylindrical Calvet-type calorimetric system Multi HTC 96 (Setaram, Caluire, France)","method":"differential scanning calorimetry (DSC)","page":2,"quote":"After testing the gas tightness of the tantalum capsules in a separate furnace, the samples were measured by differential scanning calorimetry (DSC) in a heat-flux cylindrical Calvet-type calorimetric system Multi HTC 96 (Setaram, Caluire, France). The equipment was calibrated using pure Cu, Ag and Mg sealed in tantalum capsules. Helium, at a flow rate of 2 l/h, was used as the analysis chamber gas. The reference Ta-capsule was also sealed by welding, and a sapphire cylinder was used as the reference material. The sapphire mass was 492.5 mg, which represented a good balance to the heat capacity of the sample. The samples were first heated to 700   C into the molten state with heating rate of þ10 K/ min and then cooled down/heated up in the following cycles:  5 K/ min, þ5 K/min,  1 K/min and þ1 K/min. The results were observed to be consistent and reproducible, with the difference between the corresponding heating and cooling peaks being below 4 K. The overall uncertainty of DSC measurements for temperature determination was estimated as  3 K.","second_reader_agrees":true,"stated_uncertainty":" 3 K","type":"measurement"},{"extraction_accepted":false,"has_dropped_fields":true,"id":"ORC-VSM7H5ZTA6","page":2,"quote":"The alloys were prepared from the appropriate mixtures of 99.9% pure magnesium (Shanxi Yinguang) and 99.5% pure elemental Ce, La and Nd (China Rare Metal Material Co. Ltd.) by induction melting in a mild steel crucible under a protective argon atmosphere and cast into a steel mould.","second_reader_agrees":false,"starting_materials":"99.9% pure magnesium (Shanxi Yinguang) and 99.5% pure elemental Ce, La and Nd (China Rare Metal Material Co. Ltd.)","synthesis":"induction melting in a mild steel crucible under a protective argon atmosphere and cast into a steel mould","type":"sample"},{"extraction_accepted":false,"id":"ORC-6DSHOCYRSH","label":"A1","measured_composition":"Mg-35.5Ce-4.66La","page":3,"quote":"Fig. 1. Phase identification by EDS and XRD in Mg-35.5Ce-4.66La (A1) alloy: SEM backscattered electron image and EDS compositions of phases in (a) the as-cast sample, and (b) the 500   C annealed sample, and (c) XRD spectra of both as-cast and 500   C annealed samples.","second_reader_agrees":false,"type":"sample"},{"extraction_accepted":false,"id":"ORC-OOHP5NCRAT","label":"A2","measured_composition":"Mg-37.1Ce-5.40La","page":4,"quote":"Fig. 2. Phase identification by EDS and XRD in Mg-37.1Ce-5.40La (A2) alloy: SEM backscattered electron image and EDS compositions of phases in (a) the as-cast sample, and (b) the 500   C annealed sample, and (c) XRD spectra of both as-cast and 500   C annealed samples.","second_reader_agrees":false,"type":"sample"},{"applies_to":"samples of the as-cast alloys","atmosphere_or_container":"sealed in silica tubes","cooling":"water quenching","duration":"100 h","duration_parsed":{"hours":100.0,"printed":"100 h"},"extraction_accepted":true,"id":"ORC-7IG2JODTOP","page":2,"purpose":"To determine the equilibrium phases present in the alloys","quote":"To determine the equilibrium phases present in the alloys, samples of the as-cast alloys were also sealed in silica tubes and annealed at 500   C for 100 h, followed by water quenching.","second_reader_agrees":true,"temperature":{"converted_in_code":false,"printed":"500   C"},"temperature_printed":"500   C","temperature_status":"unparsed","type":"treatment"}],"paper":"doi:10.1016/j.intermet.2012.04.012","reader_tier":"preliminary_flash","readers":["gemini-3.8-flash / exp-context-v2.1-quote","claude-opus-5.5 / exp-context-v2.1-quote (claude broker)"],"section_basis":"methods_heading"}},"elements":["LA","MG","ND"],"licence":"CC BY 4.0 (derived data; quotes under fair use)","models":{},"note":"records[].locator.ref -> artifacts; records[].model -> models (full records: orchid-literature.jsonl.gz)","papers":{"doi:10.1016/j.intermet.2012.04.012":{"authors":["Joachim Gröbner","Milan Hampl","Rainer Schmid-Fetzer","Mark A. Easton","Suming Zhu","Mark A. Gibson","Jian-Feng Nie"],"citation":"Joachim Gröbner, Milan Hampl, Rainer Schmid-Fetzer, Mark A. Easton, Suming Zhu, Mark A. Gibson et al., Phase analysis of Mg–La–Nd and Mg–La–Ce alloys, Intermetallics 28, 92-101 (2012).","container":"Intermetallics","doi":"10.1016/j.intermet.2012.04.012","doi_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.intermet.2012.04.012","id":"doi:10.1016/j.intermet.2012.04.012","kind":"corpus_paper","met